   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the county law and the tax law, in relation to authorizing the\ncounty of Tioga to impose an additional surcharge to pay for the costs\nassociated with updating the telecommunication equipment and telephone\nservices needed to provide an enhanced 911 emergency telephone system to serve\nsuch county; and providing for the repeal of such provisions upon expiration\nthereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S2031",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S2031-2021",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §337, County L; amd §186-g, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "County Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S2031\n\nSPONSOR: AKSHAR\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the county law and the tax law, in relation to authoriz-\ning the county of Tioga to impose an additional surcharge to pay for the\ncosts associated with updating the telecommunication equipment and tele-\nphone services needed to provide an enhanced 911 emergency telephone\nsystem to serve such county; and providing for the repeal of such\nprovisions upon expiration thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of the bill is to impose an additional surcharge on wireless\ncommunications and landline services to fund the county's Public Safety\nRadio Capital project. This legislation is at the request of Tioga Coun-\nty.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Section 337 of the county law is amended by authorizing Tioga\nCounty to impose a surcharge of one dollar per telecommunication line\nper month. Any local law shall state the amount of surcharge, the date\non which it begins, and the date the service begins. Any service suppli-\ner will be given a minimum of forty-five days to compose a written\nnotice prior to the date the service will begin. No surcharge shall be\nimposed upon more than seventy-five exchange access lines per customer\nper location.\n\nSection 2: Amends section 186-g of the tax law as separately amended by\nchapter 120 and 711 of the laws of 2019 in that the county of Tioga may\nimpose an additional surcharge at the rate of one dollar per month.\n\nSection 3: Amends section 186-g of the tax law, as amended by chapter\n711 of the laws of 2019 in that the county of Tioga may impose an addi-\ntional surcharge at the rate of one dollar per month.\n\nSection 4: Amends section 186-g of the tax law, as amended by section 3\nof part EEE of chapter 59 of the laws of 2017 in that the county of\nTioga may impose an additional surcharge at the rate of one dollar per\nmonth.\n\nSection 5: Establishes the effect date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nTioga County has requested (Resolution No. 292-19) legislation to impose\na surcharge on wireless communications and landline services to fund the\nCounty's Public Safety Radio Capital project. The County's Public Safety\nRadio' Capital project will address issues of outdated technology with\nnew radios and radio towers that will allow emergency personnel to\nbetter communicate with dispatch and one another.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2020 - S7618A: Referred to Local Government\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\nThis legislation will have no fiscal implications for the state. The\nfunds raised by the surcharge will be used by the county for upgrades to\nits emergency communications systems.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately and be deemed repealed ten years\nafter it shall have become a law.\n",
